Subject: [PATCH] virgl: stand in for a sampler view of another type

trynix carries this patch with 0001 for unkernel's GL renderer, and it
can go with 0001 once unkernel's vrend stops passing such bindings to
WebGL.

A draw whose shader declares a float sampler where the view's texture
has an integer format, or an integer sampler where it has a float or
normalized one, samples undefined values in GL and GLES. WebGL 2 refuses
the draw with INVALID_OPERATION ("Mismatch between texture format and
sampler type"), even when the shader never samples that view. Firefox's
WebRender makes such draws: one of its instanced draws had its RGBA32I
texture on the units of a float sampler in each stage. Mesa makes them
too, with the RGBA8 texture it puts on the unit of an integer sampler
that has no complete texture. On unkernel the first such draw puts the
guest's context in error and every later draw of it fails, so Firefox
stops drawing.

The graphics shader CSOs now keep the return type of each sampler view
the shader declares. Before a draw, a view whose texture's format does
not match its sampler's type is replaced on the host by a view of a
1x1 texture of a matching format (RGBA8, RGBA8I or RGBA8UI) and the
same target and swizzle, the way 0001 replaces a view in a feedback
loop. The real view goes back at the first draw after the views, the
framebuffer or a shader change. Only values GL leaves undefined change.

The texture's format is compared, not the view's: a GLES 3.0 host has
no texture views and samples the texture's own format.

Not covered: a shadow sampler whose texture is not a depth texture, or
whose sampler state does not compare, which WebGL 2 also refuses.

